[Music]  in 2015  i gave a series of lectures  and discussions on the theme of  understanding  anger and they were hosted by the  kingston public library in kingston new  york  who had previously invited me for a  year of monthly lectures in 2014 the  existentialism lectures that you'll find  in another playlist  and i thought what would i like to talk  about what would people be  interested in i was doing a lot of  research  at the time as i still continue to do on  the  emotion of anger how to understand it  how to manage anger how to deal with  other people's anger  how it affects politics religion  relationships everything  under the sun and i knew that there were  a lot of other people who  not only might benefit from a talk  series on anger but  also would be quite interested in it  and i had been doing research for quite  some time  on approaches to anger in  ancient and medieval and also early  modern literary philosophical  theological and  psychological and even medical treaties  there's a lot of great  analysis discussion you know sort of  empirical observation and generalization  about this troublesome emotion ranging  throughout the western tradition  and so i thought that's what i'll do a  talk series on understanding anger so  the nine  videos that you see in this playlist  those are the lecture discussion talk  whatever you want to call them  that were hosted at the kingston public  library  and you'll notice as you're watching  them that there's a lot of different  voices coming in besides of course my  own  those are the participants some of whom  were coming every s  every session some of whom were just you  know  wandering in and everybody in between  by the end of the series it had taken on  a real momentum and we had to go to  larger and larger rooms  in order to accommodate the number of  people who were coming which was quite  gratifying  and we began in a sort of chronological  way  there's different ways of doing it you  know  we we started by looking at ancient  greek  epic and tragic poetry which means their  plays  so we looked at homer we looked at  the playwrights um you know the  tragedians  and even some comedy stuff the session  after that we looked at at anger in the  hebrew scriptures particularly  in the wisdom literature where there's a  lot of analysis devoted to it because it  was a  a big problem there as well and then we  got  into philosophy we looked at  the role that anger played in various  platonic dialogues then we looked at  aristotle the first  really scientific treat treatment of  anger  where he's looking at it in multiple  ways as a physiologist  you know kind of an unusual from our  perspective anger was  boiling around the heart of the blood um  but also as a psychologist as a  political scientist  as an ethicist and then we looked at  hellenistic philosophy the stoics on  anger  epicureans on anger plutarch discussing  anger and we even started moving into  early christian and then later christian  with thomas aquinas  views on anger and the reason why  there's only nine lectures is because we  moved from kingston new york to  where we now live here in milwaukee  wisconsin  in october so that that cut the series  short otherwise it was scheduled to go  on for 12 and we were going to look at  anger in the song of roland and in  beowulf  and we're gonna move through the middle  ages and even into the early  modern period we didn't get to that i  might resume the series sometime  down the line so what you have here is  the series  as we were able to to hold it with nine  episodes to it from you know january  all the way into september  a lot of really interesting discussions  a lot of  insights that i was bringing in from  these classic  thinkers texts and uh you know we could  even say disciplines  that a philosophy that of theology that  of literature  and so i hope that you enjoy this  playlist  and that you get something out of it and  my biggest hope  is that it will lead you to read these  authors for yourself and to  you know use them not just to understand  anger but but for understanding so many  other things because each one of them is  an entire world worth exploring on your  part  so that is the understanding anger  playlist  [Music]  you

